<title>USA: Chicago city panel advances $195 mln of TIF bonds.</title>
<headline>Chicago city panel advances $195 mln of TIF bonds.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Chicago City Council panel has approved plans to issue $195 million of bonds for various projects in a downtown tax increment financing district.</p>
<p>Finance Committee members voted Thursday to recommend issuance of the series 1997 Tax Increment Allocation bonds for projects including new theater developments and an elevated train station, committee spokesman Donal Quinlan said.</p>
<p>The plan goes next to the full City Council for consideration at its July 30 meeting, Quinlan said.</p>
<p>((--David Bailey, Chicago Newsroom, 312-408-8647))</p>
